     "debunk_text": "Irregular periods are often accompanied by other physical symptoms that provide clues about what may be causing hormonal imbalance or reproductive health concerns.\n\nYou may notice:\n\n Pelvic pain or severe cramping\n Sudden acne or skin changes\n Hair thinning or excess facial hair\n Fatigue\n Mood swings\n Weight fluctuations\n Bloating\n Pain during intercourse\n Difficulty becoming pregnant\n\nTracking these symptoms can help your provider identify patterns and determine the best next steps. [...] Cycles shorter than 21 days or longer than 35 days\n Missing periods entirely\n Bleeding between periods\n Extremely heavy or unusually light flow\n Spotting throughout the month\n Periods that change dramatically from cycle to cycle\n\nAlthough occasional variation may not be concerning, consistent irregularity should not be ignored.\n\n## Why Do Irregular Periods Happen? [...] You miss three or more periods in a row\n Your cycle suddenly becomes unpredictable\n You bleed heavily enough to soak through a pad or tampon every hour\n You experience severe pain during periods\n You bleed between cycles\n Your periods stop unexpectedly and you are not pregnant\n You notice symptoms such as hair loss, fatigue, or unexplained weight changes\n\nIgnoring irregular periods may delay diagnosis of underlying conditions that could affect fertility, hormone health, or overall wellness.",
