     "debunk_text": "Women are born with all the eggs that they will ever have for their lifetime. The highest number of eggs that a woman ever had was actually before birth, when her mother was 5 months pregnant with her. At this stage of life, a woman had approximately 6-7 million eggs. Once the eggs reach this peak, they stop dividing and start dying off, so much so that at the time of birth, only 1-2 million eggs are left in the ovaries. This number decreases to 300,000-400,000 the first time a woman has her",
