     "flagged_phrase": "",
     "reason": "",
     "evidence_id": "WEB-1",
     "debunk_text": "Women are born with all the eggs they will ever have — and that number steadily declines over time.  \n  \n• At birth: ~1–2 million eggs  \n• At puberty: ~300,000–500,000 eggs  \n• Age 30: ~100,000 eggs remaining  \n• Age 37: ~25,000 eggs remaining  \n• Menopause: ~1,000 eggs or fewer  \n  \nOnly about 300–500 eggs will ever ovulate. The rest are lost naturally through a process called atresia.",
