     "debunk_text": "Throughout human history, one type of story never seems to go away: the conspiracy theory. \n\nConspiracy theories may seem like a modern epidemic — a byproduct of social media algorithms and a 24-hour news cycle. But according to Kathryn Olmsted, a distinguished professor of history at UC Davis with expertise in conspiracy theories, that isn’t the case. “They’ve been very common in the past, throughout history in all different cultures and throughout the world today,” she said.",
