     "evidence_id": "WEB-3",
     "debunk_text": "days followed by ≈4 days of close to maximal infectiousness (Li et al., 2020a; He et al., 2020). The exact durations vary among people, and some are infectious for much longer. Using R0≈4, the number of cases will quadruple every ≈7 days or double every ≈3 days. 1000-fold growth (going from one case to 103) requires 10 doublings since 210 ≈ 103; 3 days × 10 doublings = 30 days, or about one month. So we expect ≈1000x growth in one month, a million-fold (106) in two months, and a billion fold [...] ### Replication timescales\n\nVirion entry into cell (for SARS-CoV-1). (Schneider et al., 2012): \"Previous experiments had revealed that virus is internalized within 15 min\". (Ng et al., 2003): \"Within the first 10 min, some virus particles were internalized into vacuoles (arrow) that were just below the plasma membrane surface (Fig. 2, arrows). […] The observation at 15 min postinfection (p.i.), did not differ much from 10 min p.i. (Fig. 4a)\".",
