     "debunk_text": "People with COVID-19 can be infectious from 1–2 days before and up to 8–10 days after symptoms begin. The majority of transmission appears to occur during the early periods of infection, particularly in the 1–2 days before symptoms start and within the first few days of symptom onset. This period of infectiousness may be reduced slightly but has been fairly consistent since SARS-CoV-2 emerged. Individuals who are asymptomatic can also transmit the virus.",
