     "claim_text": "Finding the vaccine is totally voluntary.",
     "verdict": "FAKE_NEWS_WEB",
     "addresses": "yes",
     "stance": "asserting",
     "flagged_phrase": "Finding the vaccine is totally voluntary.",
     "reason": "The source notes that many COVID‑19 vaccine policies clearly limit choice and that mandates may be required, indicating vaccination is not totally voluntary.",
     "evidence_id": "WEB-1",
     "debunk_text": "There are important objections to this argument. First, it wrongly implies that respect for autonomy is absolute. Second, the strength of this position relies on the success of voluntary vaccination. The point of the case for vaccine mandates is that autonomy must sometimes yield to the greater good. When voluntary compliance fails to achieve near-universal immunization coverage and poses risks of harm to others, it is time to resort to mandates. Least infringement is a principle of balance but [...] spread of the more serious highly transmissible Delta variant tip the scales toward some form of mandatory vaccination policy. The extent to which voluntary compliance compared with compulsory vaccination policies promotes near-universal coverage and the related consequences of each are questions for study. [...] For proponents of autonomous choice, the ethical and prudent course is to continue to follow voluntary vaccination programs to encourage and persuade, including effective presentation of developing vaccine information with targeted educational efforts; making vaccination easily accessible (on site, with paid release time for appointments and to recover from adverse effects); child care assistance for those who need it; and committing to respect for the right of informed consent and refusal and",
     "evidence_source": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov — https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8633920",
