     "debunk_text": "use cameras to track both eyes, as seen in systems like PupilLabs . Some advanced VR headsets, such as the HTC Vive Pro Eye, incorporate integrated eye tracking sensors within the headset itself . Regardless of the system used, proper calibration is crucial to ensure accurate gaze estimation based on eye orientation [32,33,34,35]. During the calibration phase, the system establishes a relationship between the raw, uncalibrated data from the device and the real gaze points. To achieve this, [...] Image 32: Mti 08 00108 g007 [...] Image 25: Mti 08 00108 g001",
