     "evidence_id": "WEB-1",
     "debunk_text": "COVID-19 vaccines cannot cause infection: mRNA vaccines do not contain live virus, so they cannot give you COVID.\n Vaccines do not alter DNA: Messenger RNA cannot integrate into human DNA.\n No proven effect on fertility: Studies show no link between COVID-19 vaccination and infertility in women.\n Pregnant and breastfeeding women can choose vaccination: Professional organizations recommend individualized decisions in consultation with a physician. [...] ## Frequently Asked Questions\n\nNo. The COVID-19 vaccines do not contain live virus and cannot cause infection. mRNA vaccines only instruct cells to produce a harmless protein that triggers immunity.\n\nNo. Messenger RNA from the vaccine cannot be converted into DNA, so the vaccine does not alter your genetic material.\n\nThere is no evidence that COVID-19 vaccines affect fertility or female reproductive health.",
