    {
     "window": 5,
     "claim_text": "Now these articles led to social media posts claiming the COVID vaccine will contain a chip to track you.",
     "verdict": "NOT_FAKE_NEWS_WEB",
     "addresses": "yes",
     "stance": "asserting",
     "flagged_phrase": "",
     "reason": "FactCheck.org reports social‑media posts falsely claiming COVID‑19 vaccines contain a chip to track recipients.",
     "evidence_id": "WEB-1",
     "debunk_text": "“What that chip does is it has the unique serial number for each dose,” Walker said in the original interview. “It is designed so that there is no counterfeiting. It is designed so that we’ll know exactly that the right dose hasn’t expired. However, that chip only refers to the dose — there’s no personal information, no patient information. It’s simply like a barcode, only we know instantaneously where and when that dose has been used.” [...] ##### Quick Take\n\nA video circulating on social media falsely claims that vaccines for COVID-19 have a microchip that “tracks the location of the patient.” The chip, which is not currently in use, would be attached to the end of a plastic vial and provide information only about the vaccine dose. It cannot track people.\n\n##### Full Story\n\nCOVID-19 vaccines have begun rolling out, but so has misinformation about them. [...] In reality, the chip would allow those administering the vaccine to check that the dose hasn’t expired and isn’t counterfeit, Hofman said. “It’s incapable of collecting any personal information,” he said.\n\nAlso, it’s worth noting that ApiJect’s syringes aren’t being used for either the currently available vaccine developed by Pfizer and the German biotech company BioNTech or the next one up for emergency use authorization, which was developed by Moderna.",
     "evidence_source": "factcheck.org — https://www.factcheck.org/2020/12/covid-19-vaccines-dont-have-patient-tracking-devices",
     "evidence_url": "https://www.factcheck.org/2020/12/covid-19-vaccines-dont-have-patient-tracking-devices",
     "similarity": null,
     "retrieved_ids": [
      "WEB-1",
      "WEB-3",
